<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      Tauri merges this into the generated Info.plist.

      These usage descriptions are NOT optional documentation: macOS refuses to
      even PROMPT for a protected resource unless the app declares why it wants
      it. Without NSMicrophoneUsageDescription the microphone request was denied
      silently — no prompt, no error, no entry in the permission list — and
      dictation simply did nothing. Everything else had been granted, which made
      it look like a code bug rather than a missing declaration.
    -->
    <key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription</key>
    <string>HereWord records your voice so it can be transcribed to text. Audio is processed on this computer and is never uploaded or saved.</string>

    <key>NSAudioCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>HereWord can temporarily quiet other apps while recording or reading aloud. Other apps' audio is never saved or uploaded.</string>

    <!-- Typing into the focused app, reading a selection, and controlling
         supported players use Apple Events. -->
    <key>NSAppleEventsUsageDescription</key>
    <string>HereWord reads selected text, types dictated text, and controls supported music players when you choose to pause or fade their audio.</string>

    <!-- Snip and read captures a region of the screen, OCRs it locally, and
         deletes the capture immediately. -->
    <key>NSScreenCaptureUsageDescription</key>
    <string>HereWord captures the area you select so the text in it can be read aloud. The capture is deleted as soon as the text is extracted.</string>

    <!-- Menu-bar utility: no Dock icon. The settings window is opened from the
         tray, so a Dock tile would imply a main window that does not exist. -->
    <key>LSUIElement</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
